// A region in a diverging match arm, with a `return` AFTER it.
//
// The second of the two scopes `emit_simple_stmt` serves. `gen_block` publishes
// its chain into `cg` as it walks, and this walker has no republish step to undo
// that, so before the fix the region's exit outlived the region: the `return`
// re-ran `sys_seal_exit` on a token already spent. Measured `seal-balance -1
// misnest 1` — an exactly-once violation, and under AmigaOS a surplus `Enable()` with the
// caller still believing it is protected.
fn f(n: int) -> int {
    match n {
        0 => { seal { println(1); } return 10; }
        | _o => { return 20; }
    }
}
fn main() { println(f(0)); }
